>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `nitpick`

``` hol4
Refute.nitpick : term -> outcome
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Runs Refute's Nitpick-style finite model finder.

`Refute.nitpick tm` calls `Refute.refute` using `!Refute.the_config` after
forcing backend selection to `SOME ["kodkod"]`.  Every other field of the
current configuration is preserved, including finite scopes, solver and
encoding options, output controls, quiet mode, and expectations.

The `kodkod` backend is configured only when the external Kodkodi
component is available.  If it is unavailable, the result is `Unknown`
with a no-configured-backend reason.  A finite model may be `Genuine`
without a HOL certificate; clients requiring a theorem must inspect the
counterexample's `cert` field.

